**Theorem 6.2 (four individual exact original kernels on a reached chart).**
For every $V\in\{S,B,T,M_J\}$ separately and $h,k\in Z_P$,

$$
V(h)=V(k)\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad Q(h)=Q(k).
$$

Proof. Every cut of this Zero chart has a prescribed non-IN original
source row: bound RD, EX(16), WR(16,0 or sep), source MR, bound MR,
or the next original reservation-field row at the final Zero return.
The inlining retains that original row/effect on original ports; it has
not yet reached the changed final return CTL. The projection of its
complete successor to original CAP coordinates therefore includes the
current retained 13 request triple and the original meter, as well as
its other original fields. Equality of original $Q$ response maps
implies equality of this successful Advance response. The current
canonical $U(J)$ payload is still retained and unmodified, so equal
original successors give the same $J$. Their one-per-row meter receipt
counts give equal successor ordinals and hence equal predecessor
ordinals. From the common actual $P$, choice 01 and that same $J$
determine the entire intervening literal native history. Stopping at
the same ordinal gives $h=k$, including EX-before-WR and the final
delimiter-MR cut. Conversely $h=k$ gives the same original legal
domains, labels, complete successors and readouts.

For $S$, equal support decodes equal selected memory and hence equal
histories by §3, giving equal $Q$; equal $Q$ gives $h=k$ and equal
support. For $B$, prefix closure and extraction give the first implication;
equal $Q$ gives identical terminal paths for the second. For $T$, native
erasure gives equal histories and equal $Q$; equal $Q$ fixes the native
history and its compiled occurrence word. For $M_J$, extraction gives
equal histories and equal $Q$; equal $Q$ gives identical selected
backing/rights. These prove the eight chart implications separately. ∎

